Dear All

S-PLUS are pleased to announce this new course:
S-PLUS for SAS Users by Bob Burn & Mike Denham
Venue: Museum of London
Date: 10-12 September 2001

SAS is a widely used and powerful tool for data analysis with
 excellent data management capabilities.  S-PLUS is a different 
kind of package and has strengths which can effectively 
complement it.  These include facilities for data exploration, 
interactive and presentation quality graphics, modern statistical 
methods and a powerful object-orientated language for flexible 
data analysis.

This 3 day course is an introduction to S-PLUS aimed at SAS users.  
After getting familiar with the user interface, we will compare the 
ways in which the two packages manage data.

We will review methods of statistical data analysis covered by both 
packages and then explore some of the more novel features available 
in S-PLUS; for example, non-parametric regression and 
tree-based models.

Two features of S-PLUS that complement SAS nicely are interactive 
analysis and extensibility of the system.  Examples of these will be 
presented and explored.  Comparisons with SAS are made 
throughout the curse.

