The version of nlme3 compiled for S+ 2000 on nlme.stat.wisc.edu (which is
later than that shipped with S+ 2000, I believe) was compiled by me from
the sources on nlme.stat.wisc.edu.  You could do the same.
NLME is GPL-ed and all its sources are freely available.

However, ms is part of S-PLUS, not part of nlme3, and its .C calls are
to proprietary S code.

If you really need all the details, there is another version of nlme not
using ms() as part of the Open Source R project (www.r-project.org).

