You can use ISO-Latin coding in S-Plus plotted text strings going to
PostScript.  That gives you all accented characters required for
West European languages.  You can enter the characters using the octal
coding.

I'm not sure how these characters will plot on various other devices.

See help for ps.options().  This file gives the following example for
European usage:

        ps.options (paper="A4", setfont=ps.setfont.latin1)

