Hi all:

I have a question about anova.lme (latest SP2000 version of nlme library).

I created 2 simple class 'lme' objects, z1 and z2, say, via calls of form
z<-lme(fixed=...,random=..., data=indata,...).
This is done within a function and the actualcalling  procedure is a bit
more complicated, but I think irrelevant.

If, still within the function, I hard code the line:

anova(z1, z2)

things work fine. However, if I instead code:

do.call('anova',list(z1,z2))

