> are: Is it possible to move objects from the directory they were
> originally created in and still be able to see them in the Object
> Explorer, and, if so, What is the correct procedure to do so?

Move whole directories.

If all that is wrong is missing _sum files, make.DB.summary(n)
in S-PLUS will re-create them, where n is the attached position.

Deeper explanation.  On case-insensitive file systems, object names are
mapped to __XX type names, and the mapping is in ___nonfi.  The files
themselves have no meaning without reference to ___nonfi.

Object explorer/browsers need the summary files. __sum*.  They cna be
re-created.

Under some circumstances you need an empty _db3.1 file.

