>

> 1 - pchisq(g,df=deg)

>

> However,  if one runs

>

> reg11 <- update(reg1,.~. + as.factor(year)),

>

> Splus will estimate the model only for a subset of the data, the years

> for which y has values

>

> of  both 0 and 1.  So, one can run the chisquare test, however, I don't

> think the answer will be meaningful.

That's just not true.  Here's a counter-example:

y <- c(rep(0, 10), rbinom(10, 1, 0.5))

x <- 1:20

year <- rep(1990:1991, rep(10, 2))

cbind(y, x, year)

      y  x year

 [1,] 0  1 1990

 [2,] 0  2 1990

