Recent releases of S-PLUS on Unix and Windows have a utility function
called "recover.nonfiles", which lets you recover from a deleted or
corrupted ___nonfi (or ___nonfile) file.  It is not well documented,
but is pretty straightforward to use.

When the ___nonfi/___nonfile file is deleted or corrupted, the objects
are not lost, but the names of the objects are no longer available.  
The utility finds all the __xx files and one-by-one shows each object to
you and prompts you for a name.  In Windows the object pops up in a
Notepad window.  After examining the object, close the Notepad window.  
You will then be prompted for a name for that object.  Continue the
process until all recovered objects have been identified.

