if you want the sum try:
sl<-c(309,305,125,250,128)
tot<-sum(sl)

if you want to loop which does something for each value of sl, try:
sl<-c(309,305,125,250,128) 
for (i in sl) result<-somefunction(i)

OR

for (i in 1:5) results<-somefunction(sl[i])

> > vec<-c(sl1,sl2,sl3,sl4,sl5)
> > for(i in 1:5) tot<-sum(vec[i])
> > tot
> [1] 128
> 
> Why 128 but not 309+305+125+250+128? Why the first four values are ignored? 
> 

As you can see from what I said above, the loop does one operation per
value of i. Your code is summing the value of one number. The last
number summed is 128.

