From rolf at math.unb.ca  Thu Sep 13 16:32:36 2001
From: rolf at math.unb.ca (Rolf Turner)
Date: Thu, 13 Sep 2001 13:32:36 -0300
Subject: S4 classes and methods. (Was: Re: dimnames in Sparc Splus 6.0)
Message-ID: <200109131632.NAA12608@tanner.math.unb.ca>

For what it's worth, I'd like to add my voice to the concerns
recently expressed by Terry Therneau and Frank Harrell as regards the
new classes and methods structure in the S4 engine.  As far as I am
concerned a seriously wrong design decision has been made.

I have not had much experience with the new classes and methods,
having largely stuck with Splus 3.4, but I have had some need to
struggle with Splus 5.1 and have found that things that were simple
and easy to do in 3.4 were difficult-to-impossible (for me) in 5.1.
To be honest, I must confess that I really haven't got a clue what
the new classes and methods system is all about.  After running into
a glitch in something I was trying to do --- something that was
essentially trivial in 3.4 --- I was told that I needed to understand
the new classes and methods better.  I spent a good solid afternoon
trying to read the green book on this issue, and came away basically
no wiser than before.

Now I freely admit that I am not the sharpest tool in the shed, but I
am not a total thicko either, and I have considerable experience
programming in S/Splus (I was into S almost from the get-go).  If the
new classes flummox me, then I am sure that they will bring the
majority of users to a shuddering halt.

Further, if they cause difficulties for such luminaries as Therneau
and Harrell, then --- not to put too fine a point on it --- God
help the rest of us.

Unfortunately I would conjecture that it is going to be VERY
difficult to reverse the unfortunate decision to implement the new
classes and methods ``feature''.

                                        cheers,

                                                Rolf Turner
