From dsmith at insightful.com  Thu Sep 13 17:10:57 2001
From: dsmith at insightful.com (David Smith)
Date: Thu, 13 Sep 2001 10:10:57 -0700
Subject: Multiple inheritance
Message-ID: <LGEFIDJJDBKMHCAKBCOICEEGDLAA.dsmith@insightful.com>

There was one other issue I forgot to mention in my last message.  Other
than the attribute/atomic class issue, there's one other area in Sv4 where
Sv3 code might run into difficulties -- multiple inheritance.

The basic issue is this: if you have one object with class of c("foo", "lm")
and another of class c("foo", "tree"), method dispatch will not work in Sv4
as it did in Sv4. This worked in Sv3 since the method dispatch was just
based on a naming convention for functions.  In Sv4 it actually  constructs
a method dispatch table, and multiple inheritance isn't allowed in the new
class structure.

If your Sv3 code relies on multiple inheritance, some changes will be
necessary.  (This is a problem the Migration Wizard can't solve, as
mentioned in the Release Notes.)  This is an issue that arose in our own
Wavelets module, and it was solved by restructuring the class tree in a more
logical manner.

