> For those of us who haven't yet upgraded, could someone (David Smith?)
> please supply a list of the things that worked previously that won't
> work in Splus 6.0?

There's a list of backwards-compatibility issues in the release notes for
S-PLUS 6, available on the web at:

http://www.insightful.com/support/spluslatest/ReleaseNotes.htm#BackwardCompa
t

This document is quite detailed, but the main points are:

* Some functions need to be changed (e.g. class -> oldClass, log -> logb).
The migration wizard handles such changes.

* You must now assign objects local to a function before modifying them

* Atomic objects have a class.  Objects with attributes and labels have
their own class (structure and named, respectively).

* Code that relies on multiple inheritance may need modification (in
situations where objects "x" and "y" both inherit from class "c" but "x" and
"y" themselves have different classes).

# David Smith

