I applaud your efforts to maintain as much backwards-compatibility as
possible when moving to Sv4 and I don't doubt that it was a challenge.

Nonetheless, I would not categorize the "dimnames stripping" and "class"
handling changes of Splus 6.0 as "niche areas". It is an unfortunate
situation. Gary and others now face the ugly decision of laboriously
rewriting code that uses a perfectly reasonable idiom OR adopting
workarounds that make it difficult to use some of the new features of S that
Insightful/Bell Labs worked so hard to produce.

I should say, I have used Splus for 10 years and think it, and its community
of users and providers, is great. My firm has been using Splus V6.0 for our
newer code development, without major incident. However, as we migrate the
our older Splus code, I hope we do not find an incompatibility that drives
us to undertake a painful rewrite. Business is challenging enough without
having to spend time maintaining code at the same level of functionality.

