From rolf at math.unb.ca  Mon Sep 17 18:34:55 2001
From: rolf at math.unb.ca (Rolf Turner)
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 15:34:55 -0300
Subject: Dynamic loading problem solved in Splus 5.1.
Message-ID: <200109171834.PAA20311@tanner.math.unb.ca>

With a helpful nudge from Chuck Taylor at Insightful, I found
the problem.  I had ``tidied up'' Nick Fisher's code, and in
so doing introduced an error.  I had typed a line in the call
to .Fortran() as

        ``name=as.integer(something)''

when it should've been

        ``name=as.double(something)''

That'll do it to you, but apparently not ***quite*** every time!

When I fixed that, the problem disappeared.  Funny that the code worked,
even with my error in it, in Splus 3.4 and in R, but.

                                        cheers,

                                                Rolf Turner
                                                rolf at math.unb.ca

